## 🧰 1. `compute_fn!` Macro Example

Use this macro to log compute unit usage before and after critical code blocks:

```rust
use solana_program::{msg, log::sol_log_compute_units};

#[macro_export]
macro_rules! compute_fn {
    ($label:expr => $block:block) => {{
        msg!(concat!($label, " {"));
        sol_log_compute_units();
        let result = $block;
        sol_log_compute_units();
        msg!(concat!("} // ", $label));
        result
    }};
}
```

**Usage in your program:**

```rust
pub fn expensive_operation(ctx: Context<MyContext>) -> ProgramResult {
    compute_fn!("expensive_operation" => {
        // Your costly logic here
        for _ in 0..100 {
            msg!("doing work...");
        }
    });
    Ok(())
}
```

When run (on either `localnet` or `devnet`), the Solana test-validator logs will include dispatches of compute unit usage before and after the block—making bottlenecks crystal clear. ([medium.com][1], [dev.to][2])

